// the BLOCKS consumers) and every phase was cross-checked against this machine with the full physical ROM before
// being recorded (registers, PC, status, bank, ordered ports, external reads and the whole 64 KiB RAM). Error rows
// are checked errors of this machine (the original runs on with the C of MOVE.B, takes an address error or writes
// outside RAM). Long change lists and port lists are recorded as FNV-1a hashes of the whole output RAM / the ordered
// (size, address, value) port bytes. Carry after a phase is machine bookkeeping. Declared IRQ effects (72f0 wait
// resumes) are transfer_palette_banks on the RAM image; the PHASES puts must equal its RAM effect.
